Chapter: E1000Unresettable
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Kernel chapter Pci

 The part this driver actually has to work on. Damian's Intel I219-V has a
 read-only CTRL (measured 2026-08-13), so e1000-reset is discarded and the
 device is never reset. It therefore arrives in whatever state firmware and
 the manageability engine left it, which on a PCH LAN part means the
 receiver may still be running against a ring the driver knows nothing
 about.

 The failure this pins is the quiet one. Before e1000-quiesce, a bring-up
 under these two arms reported present yes, link up yes, mac valid yes and
 send accepted 1, and received NOTHING -- every aggregate healthy and the
 one thing the driver exists for silently absent. That is why the judge
 below is a received FRAME and not a status bit: no register on this path
 distinguishes a working receiver from a ring programmed underneath a live
 one.

Section: Fixtures

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

Section: Judges

 e1000-init is called ONCE and the handle threaded, which is not style. The
 model injects a fixed number of frames; a second init builds a second ring
 and the injection budget is already spent, so a judge that re-inits reads
 an empty ring and reports a broken receiver. The first version of this file
 did exactly that and blamed the driver.

  init-present : E1000Device -> Boolean
  init-present (d) = d.e-present

 Receive is the whole point. A driver that programs the ring without
 disabling the receiver first gets silence here and health everywhere else.

  recv-frame : E1000Device -> E1000RecvResult
  recv-frame (d) = e1000-poll-frame d

 The reset genuinely did not happen, and the driver must not have concluded
 otherwise. This is the row that would have caught the 08-13 misreading.

  reset-was-refused : Integer -> Boolean
  reset-was-refused (mmio) =
   let before = e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-ctrl
   in let w = e1000-write mmio e1000-reg-ctrl (bit-or before e1000-ctrl-rst)
   in e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-ctrl == before

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let scan = pci-scan-bus 0
    in act
      when e1000-find scan
        is Just (dev) -> act
          let d = e1000-init dev
          in let r = recv-frame d
          in act
            print-line-uni ("present      : " & yn (init-present d))
            print-line-uni ("ctrl refuses : " & yn (reset-was-refused (d.e-mmio)))
            print-line-uni ("recv works   : " & yn (r.r-has-frame))
            print-line-uni ("recv length  : " & show (list-length (r.r-frame)))
          end
        end
        is None -> print-line-uni ("candidate found : no")
    end
  end

